                <!-- FAQs Section -->
                <div class="card mb-4" id="faqs">
                    <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                        <h2><i class="bi bi-question-circle"></i> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="accordion" id="faqAccordion">
                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">
                                        <strong>Q1: What's the difference between mvn clean install and mvn clean package?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p><code>mvn clean package</code> creates the JAR/WAR file in the <code>target/</code> directory.</p>
                                        <p><code>mvn clean install</code> does the same but also copies the artifact to your local Maven repository (<code>~/.m2/repository</code>), making it available to other projects on your machine.</p>
                                        <p><strong>Use package</strong> for normal development. <strong>Use install</strong> when you want other local projects to depend on this project.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                                        <strong>Q2: How do I skip tests during build?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>You can skip tests in two ways:</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-bash"># Skip test execution but compile them
mvn package -DskipTests

# Skip test compilation and execution
mvn package -Dmaven.test.skip=true</code></pre>
                                        <div class="alert alert-warning mt-2">
                                            <strong>⚠️ Warning:</strong> Skipping tests is not recommended for production builds. Use only for quick local builds during development.
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                                        <strong>Q3: How do I handle dependency conflicts?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Maven uses "nearest definition" strategy. If two versions of the same dependency are found, the one closest to the project in the dependency tree wins.</p>
                                        <h6>View dependency tree:</h6>
                                        <pre><code class="language-bash">mvn dependency:tree</code></pre>
                                        <h6>Exclude transitive dependencies:</h6>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;com.example&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;some-lib&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;1.0.0&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;exclusions&gt;
        &lt;exclusion&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.unwanted&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;unwanted-lib&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;/exclusion&gt;
    &lt;/exclusions&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;</code></pre>
                                        <h6>Force a specific version:</h6>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;dependencyManagement&gt;
    &lt;dependencies&gt;
        &lt;dependency&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;com.example&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;conflicting-lib&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;version&gt;2.0.0&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/dependency&gt;
    &lt;/dependencies&gt;
&lt;/dependencyManagement&gt;</code></pre>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">
                                        <strong>Q4: What are Maven profiles and when should I use them?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Profiles allow you to customize builds for different environments (dev, test, production).</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;profiles&gt;
    &lt;profile&gt;
        &lt;id&gt;development&lt;/id&gt;
        &lt;activation&gt;
            &lt;activeByDefault&gt;true&lt;/activeByDefault&gt;
        &lt;/activation&gt;
        &lt;properties&gt;
            &lt;db.url&gt;jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/dev_db&lt;/db.url&gt;
        &lt;/properties&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;
    
    &lt;profile&gt;
        &lt;id&gt;production&lt;/id&gt;
        &lt;properties&gt;
            &lt;db.url&gt;jdbc:mysql://prod-server:3306/prod_db&lt;/db.url&gt;
        &lt;/properties&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;
&lt;/profiles&gt;</code></pre>
                                        <p>Activate a profile:</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-bash">mvn clean package -Pproduction</code></pre>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">
                                        <strong>Q5: How do I create an executable JAR with dependencies?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Use the maven-assembly-plugin or maven-shade-plugin to create a "fat JAR" with all dependencies:</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;plugin&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-shade-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;3.5.1&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;executions&gt;
        &lt;execution&gt;
            &lt;phase&gt;package&lt;/phase&gt;
            &lt;goals&gt;
                &lt;goal&gt;shade&lt;/goal&gt;
            &lt;/goals&gt;
            &lt;configuration&gt;
                &lt;transformers&gt;
                    &lt;transformer implementation="org.apache.maven.plugins.shade.resource.ManifestResourceTransformer"&gt;
                        &lt;mainClass&gt;com.library.Main&lt;/mainClass&gt;
                    &lt;/transformer&gt;
                &lt;/transformers&gt;
            &lt;/configuration&gt;
        &lt;/execution&gt;
    &lt;/executions&gt;
&lt;/plugin&gt;</code></pre>
                                        <p>This creates <code>target/library-management-system-1.0.0-shaded.jar</code> with all dependencies bundled.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq6">
                                        <strong>Q6: What's SNAPSHOT version and when to use it?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>SNAPSHOT versions indicate work in progress. Maven checks for updates to SNAPSHOT dependencies on each build.</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;version&gt;1.0.0-SNAPSHOT&lt;/version&gt;</code></pre>
                                        <div class="alert alert-info">
                                            <strong>Development:</strong> Use SNAPSHOT versions (1.0.0-SNAPSHOT)<br>
                                            <strong>Release:</strong> Use release versions (1.0.0, 1.0.1, etc.)<br>
                                            <strong>Maven behavior:</strong> SNAPSHOT versions are re-downloaded to get latest changes
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq7">
                                        <strong>Q7: How do I run Maven behind a corporate proxy?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <p>Configure proxy in <code>~/.m2/settings.xml</code>:</p>
                                        <pre><code class="language-xml">&lt;settings&gt;
    &lt;proxies&gt;
        &lt;proxy&gt;
            &lt;id&gt;corporate-proxy&lt;/id&gt;
            &lt;active&gt;true&lt;/active&gt;
            &lt;protocol&gt;http&lt;/protocol&gt;
            &lt;host&gt;proxy.company.com&lt;/host&gt;
            &lt;port&gt;8080&lt;/port&gt;
            &lt;username&gt;your-username&lt;/username&gt;
            &lt;password&gt;your-password&lt;/password&gt;
            &lt;nonProxyHosts&gt;localhost|127.0.0.1&lt;/nonProxyHosts&gt;
        &lt;/proxy&gt;
    &lt;/proxies&gt;
&lt;/settings&gt;</code></pre>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq8">
                                        <strong>Q8: What's the difference between Maven and Gradle?</strong>
                                    </button>
                                </h2>
                                <div id="faq8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        <div class="table-responsive">
                                            <table class="table table-striped">
                                                <thead>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <th>Feature</th>
                                                        <th>Maven</th>
                                                        <th>Gradle</th>
                                                    </tr>
                                                </thead>
                                                <tbody>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>Configuration</strong></td>
                                                        <td>XML (pom.xml)</td>
                                                        <td>Groovy/Kotlin DSL</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>Performance</strong></td>
                                                        <td>Good</td>
                                                        <td>Better (incremental builds)</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>Learning Curve</strong></td>
                                                        <td>Easier</td>
                                                        <td>Steeper</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>Flexibility</strong></td>
                                                        <td>Convention-based</td>
                                                        <td>Highly flexible</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>IDE Support</strong></td>
                                                        <td>Excellent</td>
                                                        <td>Excellent</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><strong>Use Case</strong></td>
                                                        <td>Enterprise Java projects</td>
                                                        <td>Android, multi-language projects</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                </tbody>
                                            </table>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

